ssification":"Music","attribute_ClassificationCode":"MUS","attribute_DeptCode":"20 - LE Music","attribute_EventInfo":"Doors: 7:30pm | Start; 8:00pm","attribute_FACMainCategory":"Music","attribute_FACSecondaryCategory":"Jazz & Blues","attribute_ForDCM":false,"attribute_IncludedInX6GroupBookingOffer":false,"attribute_ShortName":"Espen Eriksen Trio","attribute_ThirdPartyListings":false,"attribute_WebsiteCategory":"Music","attribute_ConfirmationText":"","attribute_LongEventNameLine1":"","attribute_LongEventNameLine2":"","attribute_LongEventNameLine3":"","attribute_Tutor":"","attribute_FilmCertificate":"","attribute_VideoURL":"","attribute_WebsiteCopy":"","attribute_LongEventNameLine4":"","attribute_CLVenue":"","attribute_EDIFilmNumber":"","attribute_IDRequired":"","attribute_FilmGenre":"","attribute_FILMDISTRIBUTOR":""},{"description":"Everest: The Other Side\r\n(12A) 110min | Elite ski mountaineers Jim Morrison and Hilaree Nelson fell deeply in love while reaching the pinnacle of their sport. Their drive sharpened into a shared dream: to climb and ski the direct North Face of Mount Everest -- the most difficult and dangerous climb on the mountain and the most coveted ski line on Earth. Thousands have summited the mountain via Nepal's southeast ridge, but only a handful have ever reached the top by this route -- and no one has successfully skied down. Already known for their extraordinary feats in the mountains and no strangers to loss, Morrison and Nelson stake everything on this daunting challenge.\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":110,"imageUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/breweryarts/files/08de3933-4d6b-4e1c-8fab-427dfb72118c.jpg","isOnSale":false,"name":"Everest: The Other Side","instanceDates":"27 November-27 November","thumbnailUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/breweryarts/files/08de3933-4d6b-4e1c-8fab-427dfb72118c-thumbnail.jpg","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"1150644AKNBNQMNLQBJKVBTBHPMDHDKHC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-27T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-27T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-27T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-27T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AccountCode":"4000 Ticket Sales","attribute_AreWeTheTicketAgent":false,"attribute_BreweryMember48hPriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Classification":"Cinema","attribute_ClassificationCode":"CIN","attribute_DeptCode":"12 - CIN Specialist","attribute_EDIFilmNumber":"521436","attribute_FACMainCategory":"Film","attribute_FACSecondaryCategory":"Documentary","attribute_FilmCertificate":"12A","attribute_FILMDISTRIBUTOR":"Walt Disney Pictures","attribute_FilmGenre":"DOCUMENTARY","attribute_ForDCM":true,"attribute_IncludedInX6GroupBookingOffer":false,"attribute_ShortName":"Everest: The Other Side","attribute_ThirdPartyListings":false,"attribute_VideoURL":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8gjOXAjeisY","attribute_WebsiteCategory":"Cinema","attribute_WebsiteCopy":"Elite ski mountaineers Jim Morrison and Hilaree Nelson fell deeply in love while reaching the pinnacle of their sport. Their drive sharpened into a shared dream: to climb and ski the direct North Face of Mount Everest -- the most difficult and dangerous c","attribute_EventInfo":"","attribute_ConfirmationText":"","attribute_LongEventNameLine1":"","attribute_LongEventNameLine2":"","attribute_LongEventNameLine3":"","attribute_Tutor":"","attribute_LongEventNameLine4":"","attribute_CLVenue":"","attribute_IDRequired":""},{"description":"Autumn Seasonal Family Workshop | Sat 28 Nov | Session: 2pm - 3.30pm | £8.50 | Tutor: Helena McGregor | Venue: Studio 3 | Capacity: 12 |","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"FAMILY CHRISTMAS CRAFTS: WRAPPING PAPER AND GIFT TAGS","instanceDates":"28 November-28 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"1135844ABHTQMGQKMDKRPHBKMQRSKQKMD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-28T14:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-28T14:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-28T14:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-28T14:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AccountCode":"4001 Student Fees","attribute_BreweryMember48hPriorityBooking":true,"attribute_CLVenue":"Venue: Studio 3","attribute_Classification":"Education & Outreach","attribute_ClassificationCode":"EDO","attribute_DeptCode":"30 - CL Creative Learning","attribute_EventInfo":"Session: 2pm - 3.30pm","attribute_FACMainCategory":"Visual Arts","attribute_FACSecondaryCategory":"Arts & craft","attribute_ForDCM":false,"attribute_IncludedInX6GroupBookingOffer":false,"attribute_ShortName":"Family Christmas Gifts","attribute_ThirdPartyListings":false,"attribute_Tutor":"Tutor: Helena McGregor","attribute_WebsiteCategory":"BYA","attribute_ConfirmationText":"","attribute_LongEventNameLine1":"","attribute_LongEventNameLine2":"","attribute_LongEventNameLine3":"","attribute_FilmCertificate":"","attribute_VideoURL":"","attribute_WebsiteCopy":"","attribute_LongEventNameLine4":"","attribute_EDIFilmNumber":"","attribute_IDRequired":"","attribute_FilmGenre":"","attribute_FILMDISTRIBUTOR":"","attribute_AreWeTheTicketAgent":false},{"description":"Fatherland\r\n(12A) 82min | FATHERLAND centers on the relationship between the Nobel Prize-winning writer Thomas May (Hans Zischler) and his daughter Erika (Sandra Hüller) -- actress, writer and rally driver. In the summer of 1949, at the height of the Cold War, father and daughter embark on a challenging and emotional road trip in a black Buick taking them across a Germany in ruins -- from US dominated Frankfurt to Soviet controlled Weimar. Returning home after sixteen years in exile in the US, Thomas Mann has to face not only a divided fatherland, but also a deep fracture within his own family. With FATHERLAND, Pawlikowski picks up where he left off with his award-winning IDA and COLD WAR, exploring -- in his elliptic, distilled style -- the themes of identity, family, love and guilt amid the turmoil and confusion of post-war Europe.","ht