tionText":"","attribute_LongEventNameLine1":"","attribute_LongEventNameLine2":"","attribute_LongEventNameLine3":"","attribute_FilmCertificate":"","attribute_VideoURL":"","attribute_WebsiteCopy":"","attribute_LongEventNameLine4":"","attribute_EDIFilmNumber":"","attribute_IDRequired":"","attribute_FilmGenre":"","attribute_FILMDISTRIBUTOR":"","attribute_AreWeTheTicketAgent":false},{"description":"National Theatre Live: Golden Boy\r\n(15) 180min TBC | Josh O’Connor (The Crown; Challengers) leads the cast in this searing revival of Clifford Odets’\r\nknockout American classic.\r\n1930s New York, at the height of the Depression. Joe Bonaparte is a gifted young violinist with a\r\nfuture in music, until a chance at fame and fortune lures him into the brutal world of professional\r\nboxing. He must confront what he’s willing to sacrifice, who he’s willing to become and how to find his\r\nplace in a world that demands he choose a side.\r\nBrought to life with a live string quartet and filmed live from the Almeida Theatre, Olivier Award-winner\r\nSam Yates (Vanya) directs this propulsive drama exploring ambition, identity, and the high price of\r\nsuccess.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":180,"imageUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/breweryarts/files/2d40f502-d0f2-4798-bb4a-924b2e5822d5.jpg","isOnSale":true,"name":"National Theatre Live: Golden Boy","instanceDates":"5 November-12 November","thumbnailUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/breweryarts/files/2d40f502-d0f2-4798-bb4a-924b2e5822d5-thumbnail.jpg","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"1140844AVBVKBQPTJPLGBCKCHCJKCJSMN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-05T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-05T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-12T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-12T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AccountCode":"4000 Ticket Sales","attribute_BreweryMember48hPriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Classification":"Live Screenings","attribute_ClassificationCode":"THE","attribute_DeptCode":"13 - CIN Stage on Screen","attribute_EDIFilmNumber":"352637","attribute_FACMainCategory":"Film","attribute_FACSecondaryCategory":"Performances on screen","attribute_FilmCertificate":"15","attribute_FILMDISTRIBUTOR":"National Theatre Live","attribute_FilmGenre":"THEATRE","attribute_ForDCM":true,"attribute_IDRequired":"Proof of age ID may be requested","attribute_IncludedInX6GroupBookingOffer":false,"attribute_ShortName":"NT Live: Golden Boy","attribute_ThirdPartyListings":false,"attribute_VideoURL":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hCS4Y_MBhuo","attribute_WebsiteCategory":"Cinema","attribute_WebsiteCopy":"Josh O’Connor (The Crown; Challengers) leads the cast in this searing revival of Clifford Odets’ knockout American classic. 1930s New York, at the height of the Depression. Joe Bonaparte is a gifted young violinist with a future in music, until a chance a","attribute_EventInfo":"","attribute_ConfirmationText":"","attribute_LongEventNameLine1":"","attribute_LongEventNameLine2":"","attribute_LongEventNameLine3":"","attribute_Tutor":"","attribute_LongEventNameLine4":"","attribute_CLVenue":"","attribute_AreWeTheTicketAgent":false},{"description":"Music Gig | Theatre | Rock/Pop | Doors: 7:30pm | Start: 8:00pm | Tickets: £27.50 | Staff Comps OK | £33.50 on door]","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"NEARLY DAN THE SPIRIT & SOUND OF STEELY DAN 30TH ANNIVERSARY TOUR","instanceDates":"10 April-10 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"1144644ATSRTNNCNSRPDCLPQSQDCTGBVG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2027-04-10T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-04-10T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-04-10T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-04-10T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AccountCode":"4000 Ticket Sales","attribute_AreWeTheTicketAgent":false,"attribute_BreweryMember48hPriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Classification":"Music","attribute_ClassificationCode":"MUS","attribute_DeptCode":"20 - LE Music","attribute_EventInfo":"Doors: 7:30pm | Start: 8:00pm","attribute_FACMainCategory":"Music","attribute_FACSecondaryCategory":"Music","attribute_ForDCM":false,"attribute_IncludedInX6GroupBookingOffer":false,"attribute_LongEventNameLine1":"The Spirit & Sound of Steely Dan","attribute_LongEventNameLine2":"30th Anniversary","attribute_ShortName":"Nearly Dan ","attribute_ThirdPartyListings":false,"attribute_WebsiteCategory":"Music","attribute_ConfirmationText":"","attribute_LongEventNameLine3":"","attribute_Tutor":"","attribute_FilmCertificate":"","attribute_VideoURL":"","attribute_WebsiteCopy":"","attribute_LongEventNameLine4":"","attribute_CLVenue":"","attribute_EDIFilmNumber":"","attribute_IDRequired":"","attribute_FilmGenre":"","attribute_FILMDISTRIBUTOR":""},{"description":"North Sea, Nature Untamed\r\n(U) 90min | A spectacular underwater world unknown to most…\r\n\r\nPETER VAN RODIJNEN has travelled the world, capturing breathtaking footage of some of the most spectacular oceans but has never been drawn to what he saw as the cold, lifeless grey waters of his native North Sea. All this changes when he is sent on assignment to Denmark to film the spawning of the majestic Atlantic salmon.\r\n​\r\nAfter an absence of more than 60 years, these great ocean icons are returning once again to European waters. This experience urges Peter to go out and learn more about the secrets of this little-known world.\r\n\r\n\r\nAs Peter embarks on his journey, he faces a number of challenges. He encounters dangerous currents, poor visibility and fierce storms, but his determination to uncover the secrets of this untamed natural wonder never wavers.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/breweryarts/files/36605227-b8d4-4a0c-9d5c-6aae83023fe3.jpg","isOnSale":true,"name":"North Sea, Nature Untamed","instanceDates":"1 November-5 November","thumbnailUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/breweryarts/files/36605227-b8d4-4a0c-9d5c-6aae83023fe3-thumbnail.jpg","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"1148444AQNMPVKQQLKMRHRGDKDDCBNLCV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-01T16:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-01T16:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-05T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-05T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AccountCode":"4000 Ticket Sales","attribute_AreWeTheTicketAgent":false,"attribute_BreweryMember48hPriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Classification":"Cinema","attribute_ClassificationCode":"CIN","attribute_DeptCode":"12 - CIN Specialist","attribute_EDIFilmNumber":"526509","attribute_FACMainCategory":"Film","attribute_FACSecondaryCategory":"Documentary","attribute_FilmCertificate":"U","attribute_FILMDISTRIBUTOR":"Dartmouth Films","attribute_FilmGenre":"DOCUMENTARY","attribute_ForDCM":true,"attribute_IncludedInX6GroupBookingOffer":false,"attribute_ShortName":"North Sea, Nature Untamed","attribute_ThirdPartyListings":false,"attribute_VideoURL":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CxMa-AyVJ7M","attribute_WebsiteCategory":"Cinema","attribute_WebsiteCopy":"A spectacular underwater world unknown to most…  PETER VAN RODIJNEN has travelled the world, capturing breathtaking footage of some of the most spectacular oceans but has never been drawn to what he saw as the cold, lifeless grey waters of his native Nort","attribute_EventInfo":"","attribute_ConfirmationText":"","attribute_LongEventNameLine1":"","attribute_LongEventNameLine2":"","attribute_LongEventNameLine3":"","attribute_Tutor":"","attribute_LongEventNameLine4":"","attribute_CLVenue":"","attribute_IDRequired":""},{"description":"Music HIRE | Malt Room Standing | Doors 7.30pm | Start 8pm |Tickets £31 | Age Guidance 16+ | 10% off for booking of 6 or more applies","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"ONE NIGHT IN NASHVILLE","instanceDates":"12 February-12 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"1124244ASKCHPJVGKCBQKCJQMLTLLJQDG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2027-02-12T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-02-12T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-02-12T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-02-12T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AccountCode":"2101 Music Hires - Holding Account","attribute_BreweryMember48hPriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Classification":"Music","attribute_ClassificationCode":"MUSIC HIRE","attribute_ConfirmationText":"Age Guidance 16+","attribute_DeptCode":"0","attribute_EventInfo":"Doors 7.30pm | Start 8pm","attribute_FACMainCategory":"Music","attribute_FACSecondaryCategory":"Music","attribute_ForDCM":false,"attribute_IncludedInX6GroupBookingOffer":true,"attribute_ShortName":"One Night in Nashville","attribute_ThirdPartyListings":false,"attribute_WebsiteCategory":"Music","attribute_LongEventNameLine1":"","attribute_LongEventNameLine2":"","attribute_LongEventNameLine3":"","attribute_Tutor":"","attribute_FilmCertificate":"","attribute_VideoURL":"","attribute_WebsiteCopy":"","attribute_LongEventNameLine4":"","attribute_CLVenue":"","attribute_EDIFilmNumber":"","attribute_IDRequired":"","attribute_FilmGenre":"","attribute_FILMDISTRIBUTOR":"","attribute_AreWeTheTicketAgent":false},{"description":"Onwards and Sideways\r\n(15) 115min | Tony Evans is deputy head of a primary school. Emma Dretzin is a musician and composer, and single mother of two daughters. \r\nNeither knows the other. Until a startling encounter changes the course of their lives. \r\nOn the same morning, these two are simultaneously confronted with a diagnosis of Parkinson’s Disease.\r\nThis film is the story of Tony and Emma - a friendship which unfolds unexpectedly. A story of humour and emotion, of challenge and bravado, of music and dance - transcending the assumptions of a little understood condition, and triumphing over the odds to find joy, release and love.\r\nA powerful, life-affirming British drama from Academy Award-nominated Director John Madden (Shakespeare in Love, The Best Exotic Marigold Hotel), Onwards and Sideways stars BAFTA Award-winner Rhys Ifans (Inheritance, House of the Dragon), Academy Award-nominee Laura Linney (Ozark, Love Actually), Monica Dolan (Mr Bates vs The Post Office, Sherwood), and Rory Kinnear (The Diplomat, The Lord of the Rings: Rings of Power).","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":115,"imageUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/breweryarts/files/ed10b4f8-cf73-48b0-9d0f-4052a360cdb1.jpg","isOnSale":true,"name":"Onwards and Sideways","instanceDates":"6 November-12 November","thumbnailUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/breweryarts/files/ed10b4f8-cf73-48b0-9d0f-4052a360cdb1-thumbnail.jpg","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"1155044AGGQVNLLDNNRDNTRGRPPNDCTML","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-06T13:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-06T13:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-12T16:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-12T16:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AccountCode":"4000 Ticket Sales","attribute_AreWeTheTicketAgent":false,"attribute_BreweryMember48hPriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Classification":"Cinema","attribute_ClassificationCode":"CIN","attribute_DeptCode":"12 - CIN Specialist","attribute_EDIFilmNumber":"526508","attribute_FACMainCategory":"Film","attribute_FACSecondaryCategory":"Drama","attribute_FilmCertificate":"15","attribute_FILMDISTRIBUTOR":"Jade Films","attribute_FilmGenre":"DRAMA","attribute_ForDCM":true,"attribute_IDRequired":"Proof of age ID may be requested","attribute_IncludedInX6GroupBookingOffer":false,"attribute_ShortName":"Onwards and Sideways","attribute_ThirdPartyListings":false,"attribute_VideoURL":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MR5Nkdndv18","attribute_WebsiteCategory":"Cinema","attribute_WebsiteCopy":"Tony Evans is deputy head of a primary school. Emma Dretzin is a musician and composer, and single mother of two daughters.  Neither knows the other. Until a startling encounter changes the course of their lives.  On the same morning, these two are simult","attribute_EventInfo":"","attribute_ConfirmationText":"","attribute_LongEventNameLine1":"","attribute_LongEventNameLine2":"","attribute_LongEventNameLine3":"","attribute_Tutor":"","attribute_LongEventNameLine4":"","attribute_CLVenue":""},{"description":"Otello - The Met Opera\r\n(12A) 201min | Encore | One of today’s leading dramatic tenors, Brian Jagde, takes on the tour-de-force title role of what many consider the ultimate Italian opera, live to cinemas worldwide. Verdi’s monumental Shakespearean tragedy also features soprano Ailyn Pérez in her company role debut as the long-suffering Desdemona, alongside baritone Artur Ruciński as the sinister Iago. Michele Mariotti leads the full forces of the Met Orchestra and Chorus in the exhilarating score.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":201,"imageUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/breweryarts/files/a33b552b-52af-42b1-b8d8-b041190efc52.jpg","isOnSale":true,"name":"Otello - The Met Opera","instanceDates":"27 April-27 April","thumbnailUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/breweryarts/files/a33b552b-52af-42b1-b8d8-b041190efc52-thumbnail.jpg","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"1136444AKBVMVVKKQTRHPRSMPDCVPTBCC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2027-04-27T18:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-04-27T17:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-04-27T18:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-04-27T17:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AccountCode":"4000 Ticket Sales","attribute_BreweryMember48hPriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Classification":"Live Screenings","attribute_ClassificationCode":"THE","attribute_DeptCode":"13 - CIN Stage on Screen","attribute_EDIFilmNumber":"512060","attribute_FACMainCategory":"Film","attribute_FACSecondaryCategory":"Performances on screen","attribute_FilmCertificate":"12A","attribute_FILMDISTRIBUTOR":"Trafalgar Releasing","attribute_FilmGenre":"THEATRE","attribute_ForDCM":true,"attribute_IncludedInX6GroupBookingOffer":false,"attribute_ShortName":"Otello The Met Opera","attribute_ThirdPartyListings":false,"attribute_WebsiteCategory":"Cinema","attribute_WebsiteCopy":"One of today’s leading dramatic tenors, Brian Jagde, takes on the tour-de-force title role of what many consider the ultimate Italian opera, live to cinemas worldwide. Verdi’s monumental Shakespearean tragedy also features soprano Ailyn Pérez in her compa","attribute_EventInfo":"","attribute_ConfirmationText":"","attribute_LongEventNameLine1":"","attribute_LongEventNameLine2":"","attribute_LongEventNameLine3":"","attribute_Tutor":"","attribute_VideoURL":"","attribute_LongEventNameLine4":"","attribute_CLVenue":"","attribute_IDRequired":"","attribute_AreWeTheTicketAgent":false},{"description":"(18) 90min Inc. intro (60mins & Q&A 30mins) | On 29th January 1997 Chris Morris’ current affairs satire Brass Eye was first unleashed on an unsuspecting television audience. Thirty years later it’s director, Michael Cumming, begins a tour of his cult film Oxide Ghosts: The Brass Eye Tapes.\r\n\r\nMade from hundreds of hours of unseen and behind the scenes footage from his personal archive, and only ever screened at live events, Oxide Ghosts shares insights into the process of making the ground-breaking TV series Brass Eye. Michael directed the series and pilots and, over a two-year period, witnessed the highs and lows from a very personal perspective. The film carries the blessing of Chris Morris and provides a unique glimpse of his extraordinary working practices. \r\n\r\nAt these special anniversary shows, Michael will be on hand for a Q&A after the film. This event is a must for fans of the series but will appeal to anyone with a curiosity about how great comedy is made.\r\n\r\nMichael Cumming is a director & filmmaker whose back catalogue - aside from Brass Eye - contains such gems as Snuff Box, Mark Thomas Product, Mark Steel Lectures, Matt Berry’s multi-award winning sitcom, Toast Of London and the Stewart Lee fronted, anti-rockumentary film, King Rocker.\r\n\r\n‘Oxide Ghosts offers a well-judged and very rare insight into Brass Eye’s making, encapsulating the fun and covert excitement that went on while the project was still under wraps, before all the legal wrangling kicked in. If you're an admirer of the show and the opportunity should arise for you to see Oxide Ghosts, have some self re-cocking-spect and do so without hesitation' – Andy Murray, Chortle \r\n\r\n‘In honour of the Brass Eye birthday there have been tributes published and repeats scheduled, but the surprise popularity of an almost unpublicised touring event, called Oxide Ghosts: The Brass Eye Tapes, perhaps says even more about the enduring influence of the show. Oxide Ghosts has been quietly selling out in independent cinemas across the land’ – Vanessa Thorpe, The Guardian\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Oxide Ghosts: The Brass Eye Tapes - with Director Q&A ","instanceDates":"3 February-3 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"369643AQLTJNKMBMQQPJKMBTDNSNGQHML","firstInstanceDateTime":"2027-02-03T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-02-03T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-02-03T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-02-03T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AccountCode":"4000 Ticket Sales","attribute_AreWeTheTicketAgent":false,"attribute_BreweryMember48hPriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Classification":"Cinema","attribute_ClassificationCode":"CIN","attribute_DeptCode":"12 - CIN Specialist","attribute_FACMainCategory":"Film","attribute_FACSecondaryCategory":"Documentary","attribute_FilmCertificate":"18","attribute_FILMDISTRIBUTOR":"-","attribute_FilmGenre":"DOCUMENTARY","attribute_ForDCM":false,"attribute_IDRequired":"Proof of age ID may be requested","attribute_IncludedInX6GroupBookingOffer":false,"attribute_ShortName":"Oxide Ghosts","attribute_ThirdPartyListings":false,"attribute_WebsiteCategory":"Cinema","attribute_WebsiteCopy":"On 29th January 1997 Chris Morris’ current affairs satire Brass Eye was first unleashed on an unsuspecting television audience. Thirty years later it’s director, Michael Cumming, begins a tour of his cult film Oxide Ghosts: The Brass Eye Tapes.  Made from","attribute_EventInfo":"","attribute_ConfirmationText":"","attribute_LongEventNameLine1":"","attribute_LongEventNameLine2":"","attribute_LongEventNameLine3":"","attribute_Tutor":"","attribute_VideoURL":"","attribute_LongEventNameLine4":"","attribute_CLVenue":"","attribute_EDIFilmNumber":""},{"description":"Cinema Rewind\r\nPan’s Labyrinth (20th Anniversary 4K Restoration)\r\n(15) 122min TBC |\r\nIn post–civil war Spain, 10-year-old Ofelia moves with her pregnant mother to live under the control of her cruel stepfather. Drawn into a mysterious labyrinth, she meets a faun who reveals that she may be a lost princess from an underground kingdom. To return to her true father, she must complete a series of surreal and perilous tasks that blur the line between reality and fantasy.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":121,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Pan's Labyrinth (20th Anniversary 4K Restoration)","instanceDates":"17 November-17 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"331ATKHVTVJVTTVCDVJLGSBBLQGPGGHDT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-17T19:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-17T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-17T19:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-17T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AccountCode":"4100","attribute_AreWeTheTicketAgent":false,"attribute_BreweryMember48hPriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Classification":"Cinema","attribute_ClassificationCode":"CIN","attribute_DeptCode":"12 - CIN Specialist","attribute_EDIFilmNumber":"511386","attribute_FACMainCategory":"Film","attribute_FACSecondaryCategory":"Horror","attribute_FilmCertificate":"15","attribute_FILMDISTRIBUTOR":"Studiocanal","attribute_FilmGenre":"HORROR","attribute_ForDCM":true,"attribute_IDRequired":"Proof of age ID may be requested","attribute_IncludedI